{
  "source_text": "Sacks viewed Amodei's decision to attend the World Economic Forum over Trump's second inauguration; his  hiring  of  Biden  officials;  and  Anthropic's  association  with  the  philanthropic  initiative  Open Philanthropy as evidence that Anthropic would not support Trump's agenda. [15] In October 2025, Sacks stated that  Anthropic was \"running a sophisticated regulatory capture strategy based on fearmongering.\" [16] That month, Amodei published a blog post rebuffing \"inaccurate claims\" from the Trump administration  on  Anthropic's  policies,  intensifying  the  dispute.  Amodei's  statement  included  views explicitly espoused by vice president JD Vance. [17]  In December, Amodei met with Trump officials and several senators in an effort to improve Anthropic's relationship with the Trump administration. [18]",
  "source_text_sha256": "c608ac71f813d95607a005494b5cc90fb949590778631fcec2e34bf09e57327a",
